[{:db/id "q-314895/field-1/2a376cbdcf8b7952a5dc13ba1a54d6d6c2b760f79483ad01c9e52db42bdced12" :answer/id #uuid "ae872bb6-20cb-51ac-b091-d6b7c3af38e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "11.8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-314895/field-1/6b862387b134a0a19c5423934ccde2f579b500c83f6b591c93b48e1e343da4d8" :answer/id #uuid "be37bf7e-ddbe-53a2-8a8b-9c225539a6b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12.2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-314895/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "f3f19bba-2bca-54cb-9847-9655721fb279" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-314895/field-1/2a376cbdcf8b7952a5dc13ba1a54d6d6c2b760f79483ad01c9e52db42bdced12" :answer-field/choices ["q-314895/field-1/2a376cbdcf8b7952a5dc13ba1a54d6d6c2b760f79483ad01c9e52db42bdced12" "q-314895/field-1/6b862387b134a0a19c5423934ccde2f579b500c83f6b591c93b48e1e343da4d8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-314895" :question/id #uuid "a851630a-e575-5647-a3d4-704a604c24b5" :question/math-academy-id "q-314895" :question/problem "An environmental researcher is tracking the depth $d$, in meters, of a lake during a dry season. The following table shows the rate at which the depth is decreasing.\n\n| **$t\\,\\text{(weeks)}$** | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${d}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{(meters/week)}$ | $-0.3$ | $-0.5$ | $-0.8$ | $-1.0$ |\n\nAt $t=2,$ the lake depth was $12$ meters. Use the tangent line approximation of $d$ at time $t=2$ to estimate the depth of the lake at $t=2.4.$ Do not round the answer.\n\nThe depth of the lake at $t=2.4$ weeks is estimated to be\n{{field-1}}\nmeters." :question/worked-solution "The tangent line approximation of $d(t)$ at the point $a=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(t) & =d(a)+{d}^{′}(a)(t-a) \\\\  & =d(2)+{d}^{′}(2)(t-2) \\\\  & =12+(-0.5)(t-2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can approximate $d(2.4)$ by evaluating the tangent line approximation at $t=2.4.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d(2.4) & ≈L(2.4) \\\\  & =12+(-0.5)(2.4-2) \\\\  & =12+(-0.5)(0.4) \\\\  & =12-0.2 \\\\  & =11.8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe depth of the lake at $t=2.4$ weeks is estimated to be $11.8$ meters." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-314895/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b08650da-89e7-5a9d-89a6-de3623344662"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-314895"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-346048/field-1/68c1f5bad2f62c905b0b1581cb8eb4637d3294a430200a0942ac02a7b3981344" :answer/id #uuid "633aba20-719b-51ce-9fb6-a0cee64fcd7a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "59.9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-346048/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "6090a856-99b8-5505-8fcd-24e8d8420ff8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-346048/field-1/68c1f5bad2f62c905b0b1581cb8eb4637d3294a430200a0942ac02a7b3981344" :answer-field/choices ["q-346048/field-1/68c1f5bad2f62c905b0b1581cb8eb4637d3294a430200a0942ac02a7b3981344"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-346048" :question/id #uuid "2c54b5e6-e3dd-54da-8937-f4265f08e3df" :question/math-academy-id "q-346048" :question/problem "An engineer measures the amount of fuel $F$, in liters, remaining in a generator. The following table shows the rate at which fuel is being consumed.\n\n| **$t\\,\\text{(hours)}$** | $2$ | $4$ | $6$ | $8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${F}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{(liters/hour)}$ | $-3.1$ | $-3.5$ | $-4.0$ | $-4.4$ |\n\nAt $t=4,$ the generator contained $62$ liters of fuel. Use the tangent line approximation of $F$ at time $t=4$ to estimate the amount of fuel remaining at $t=4.6.$  Do not round the answer.\n\nThe amount of fuel remaining at $t=4.6$ hours is estimated to be\n{{field-1}}\nliters." :question/worked-solution "The tangent line approximation of $F(t)$ at the point $a=4$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(t) & =F(a)+{F}^{′}(a)(t-a) \\\\  & =F(4)+{F}^{′}(4)(t-4) \\\\  & =62-3.5(t-4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can approximate $F(4.6)$ by evaluating the tangent line approximation at $t=4.6.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(4.6) & ≈L(4.6) \\\\  & =62-3.5(4.6-4) \\\\  & =62-3.5(0.6) \\\\  & =62-2.1 \\\\  & =59.9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe amount of fuel remaining at $t=4.6$ hours is estimated to be $59.9$ liters." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-346048/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b08650da-89e7-5a9d-89a6-de3623344662"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-346048"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-346036/field-1/7da1dd298cfcc84d7395b55638b7e0c61f97cb23e78528ed0aa4713f7c17e40a" :answer/id #uuid "eb6b07b1-c8c1-596d-b7ca-b35846843457" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-346036/field-1/337159745041b1c24606244465f5294adbef0dd0c451f22c8e3d1d26409da9f8" :answer/id #uuid "52005496-ebc2-5acf-bce1-7563f9f998a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-346036/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "4f26b0b1-c712-5e74-96be-9a5cf42f39f1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-346036/field-1/7da1dd298cfcc84d7395b55638b7e0c61f97cb23e78528ed0aa4713f7c17e40a" :answer-field/choices ["q-346036/field-1/7da1dd298cfcc84d7395b55638b7e0c61f97cb23e78528ed0aa4713f7c17e40a" "q-346036/field-1/337159745041b1c24606244465f5294adbef0dd0c451f22c8e3d1d26409da9f8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-346036" :question/id #uuid "77ab9b9d-0ecd-5343-b696-e422b900c37f" :question/math-academy-id "q-346036" :question/problem "The graph of the function $f(x)$ passes through $(1,-4)$ and ${f}^{′}(1)=2.$ Determine $L(x),$ the tangent line approximation of $f(x)$ at $x=1.$\n\n$L(x)=$  \n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Since the graph of $f(x)$ passes through $(1,-4)$, we have that $f(1)=-4.$ Therefore, the tangent line approximation of $f(x)$ at $a=1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(x) & =f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a) \\\\  & =f(1)+{f}^{′}(1)(x-1) \\\\  & =-4+2(x-1) \\\\  & =-4+2x-2 \\\\  & =2x-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-346036/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b08650da-89e7-5a9d-89a6-de3623344662"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-346036"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-346041/field-1/59afba529b533d43da0939a1f2e3244430951f512675b31bbaaa22a58d5faf55" :answer/id #uuid "b132dd43-c97b-5375-8fa6-4ffef4269891" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-346041/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "af13bb07-56c7-5561-8a85-b2bf26e7eacd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-346041/field-1/59afba529b533d43da0939a1f2e3244430951f512675b31bbaaa22a58d5faf55" :answer-field/choices ["q-346041/field-1/59afba529b533d43da0939a1f2e3244430951f512675b31bbaaa22a58d5faf55"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-346041" :question/id #uuid "e2a7cae9-7560-5abc-9ffc-268aee1f95ce" :question/math-academy-id "q-346041" :question/problem "Suppose that $f(-4)=1$ and ${f}^{′}(-4)=6.$ Using the tangent line approximation of $f(x)$ at $x=-4,$ estimate the value of $f(-3.8).$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$f(-3.8)≈$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The tangent line approximation of $f(x)$ at the point $a=-4$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(x) & =f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a) \\\\  & =f(-4)+{f}^{′}(-4)(x-(-4)) \\\\  & =1+6(x+4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can approximate $f(-3.8)$ by evaluating the tangent line approximation at $x=-3.8.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-3.8) & ≈L(-3.8) \\\\  & =1+6(-3.8+4) \\\\  & =1+6(0.2) \\\\  & =1+1.2 \\\\  & =2.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-346041/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b08650da-89e7-5a9d-89a6-de3623344662"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-346041"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-346037/field-1/3eb24befc3ed964ee800b2b5ca3348ca5866197b92a03aa054e0d7f2c285f3d2" :answer/id #uuid "b1fc73a2-9845-5f12-af49-878b7ec95093" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4x-9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-346037/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "5a71a790-ed1f-517c-886e-f361328170f0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-346037/field-1/3eb24befc3ed964ee800b2b5ca3348ca5866197b92a03aa054e0d7f2c285f3d2" :answer-field/choices ["q-346037/field-1/3eb24befc3ed964ee800b2b5ca3348ca5866197b92a03aa054e0d7f2c285f3d2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-346037" :question/id #uuid "9f47ed8c-7e7e-507f-892b-0c4b2ee6e7b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-346037" :question/problem "The graph of the function $f(x)$ passes through $(2,-1)$ and ${f}^{′}(2)=4.$ Determine $L(x),$ the tangent line approximation of $f(x)$ at $x=2.$\n\n$L(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Since the graph of $f(x)$ passes through $(2,-1)$, we have that $f(2)=-1.$ Therefore, the tangent line approximation of $f(x)$ at $a=2$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(x) & =f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a) \\\\  & =f(2)+{f}^{′}(2)(x-2) \\\\  & =-1+4(x-2) \\\\  & =-1+4x-8 \\\\  & =4x-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-346037/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b08650da-89e7-5a9d-89a6-de3623344662"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-346037"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-4870/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "1cb5b26a-d205-5082-b6a8-29be67e7f4f0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-4870/selection/478cbf1ea235fbfb5b60a0837fffa0a678f83a3bcb8f958a024b0760ea2175ce" :answer/id #uuid "c6854e5e-fc8d-5381-aa60-0003f954e84a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "11" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-4870/selection/12b7d840a997b0af25896f37c76d366155c72a970c1525c62ec119b69786f393" :answer/id #uuid "2a86328f-eb6b-5371-9fde-89f81df0e2a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "13" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-4870/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "f34ba620-8fa2-585c-8f86-888781029b39" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-4870/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer/id #uuid "e080f980-bd8b-51a2-a39d-27b616531ec8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-4870/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "15dd3811-2d91-59b7-8faa-943b788a766e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-4870/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer-field/choices ["q-4870/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-4870/selection/478cbf1ea235fbfb5b60a0837fffa0a678f83a3bcb8f958a024b0760ea2175ce" "q-4870/selection/12b7d840a997b0af25896f37c76d366155c72a970c1525c62ec119b69786f393" "q-4870/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-4870/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-4870" :question/id #uuid "43d17459-991b-5007-8261-da90da53334c" :question/math-academy-id "q-4870" :question/problem "Let $f$ be a function such that ${f}^{′}(x)=(2x-3)^{2}(x-1)^{4}$ and $f(0)=-2.$ Use the tangent line approximation of $f(x)$ at $x=0$ to estimate the value of $f(1).$" :question/worked-solution "The tangent line approximation of $f(x)$ at the point $a=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(x) & =f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a) \\\\  & =f(0)+{f}^{′}(0)(x-0) \\\\  & =f(0)+{f}^{′}(0)x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that $f(0)=-2,$ and since ${f}^{′}(x)==(2x-3)^{2}(x-1)^{4},$ then ${f}^{′}(0)==(2(0)-3)^{2}(0-1)^{4}=9.$ So, the tangent line approximation is given by\n\n$$\nL(x)=-2+9x.\n$$\n\nNow, we can approximate $f(1)$ by evaluating the tangent line approximation at $x=1.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1) & ≈L(1) \\\\  & =-2+9(1) \\\\  & =-2+9 \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-4870/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1b0dd714-5bf1-573f-9ff9-11802622ce92"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-4870"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-115608/selection/cadf76b3c9ea81d49a7c0215bbafd960b57c9361c98f1ffb78838a079e98a76e" :answer/id #uuid "10ee60cb-df30-5049-a0a0-0ba248a66eb2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115608/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" :answer/id #uuid "3a410dcd-4bc7-5e3c-909e-48d27f273e26" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115608/selection/ffd704be79793605a5c6e25a771da0e0eadbaf3fa7636f6ae79801bf9882c8e3" :answer/id #uuid "ddb6b211-0b35-50b1-ac58-7255af910024" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-14.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115608/selection/f509030681214332b5989836fe0af4b2eb5858d193e689fd8441dff5cd45ff45" :answer/id #uuid "ca4dbf67-af54-56b7-b10e-5898b7a4a000" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115608/selection/dfd5f31d881889706cf6a223c90e51452850b5a5fea00254db5c20ed13cc8a7f" :answer/id #uuid "b94f95e5-8142-55ce-9622-a3813734ae16" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115608/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "61d634dc-ad34-5150-80cb-4c224420b4f3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-115608/selection/dfd5f31d881889706cf6a223c90e51452850b5a5fea00254db5c20ed13cc8a7f" :answer-field/choices ["q-115608/selection/cadf76b3c9ea81d49a7c0215bbafd960b57c9361c98f1ffb78838a079e98a76e" "q-115608/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" "q-115608/selection/ffd704be79793605a5c6e25a771da0e0eadbaf3fa7636f6ae79801bf9882c8e3" "q-115608/selection/f509030681214332b5989836fe0af4b2eb5858d193e689fd8441dff5cd45ff45" "q-115608/selection/dfd5f31d881889706cf6a223c90e51452850b5a5fea00254db5c20ed13cc8a7f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-115608" :question/id #uuid "6a4c269f-3735-5033-b5a4-053c4a35fad1" :question/math-academy-id "q-115608" :question/problem "Let $f$ be a function such that ${f}^{′}(x)={x}^{2}(4x-9)$ and $f(1)=-2.$ Use the tangent line approximation of $f(x)$ at $x=1$ to estimate the value of $f(1.5).$" :question/worked-solution "The tangent line approximation of $f(x)$ at the point $a=1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(x) & =f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a) \\\\  & =f(1)+{f}^{′}(1)(x-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that $f(1)=-2,$ and since ${f}^{′}(x)={x}^{2}(4x-9),$ then ${f}^{′}(1)={1}^{2}(4\\cdot 1-9)=-5.$ So, the tangent line approximation is given by\n\n$$\nL(x)=-2-5(x-1).\n$$\n\nNow, we can approximate $f(1.5)$ by evaluating the tangent line approximation at $x=1.5.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1.5) & ≈L(1.5) \\\\  & =-2-5(1.5-1) \\\\  & =-2-5(0.5) \\\\  & =-2-2.5 \\\\  & =-4.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-115608/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1b0dd714-5bf1-573f-9ff9-11802622ce92"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-115608"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-4813/selection/c05c767eb6742c0374517cb95a1cb5ab75783e23695ee9766c8351f9373f513d" :answer/id #uuid "c7426655-66fa-5dc3-976a-d4115ca2a347" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8.75" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-4813/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" :answer/id #uuid "fba61e60-7952-5c9e-bdf0-8dab9b2cb3a9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-4813/selection/6758fbe0e699c4cf143d83ed08d339b0f33c0dcff4e60925d8c2187184bd9694" :answer/id #uuid "86fe3eb4-3907-5cda-8cc9-b7f33d978104" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9.25" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-4813/selection/f7ec98ce0d2d5e0413aaea93f098b04337f2217a14eff2f5b611bfb2fc659059" :answer/id #uuid "5f7d46f8-0a98-546d-b83f-453f8582a926" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-4813/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "1b323b3c-741e-5993-bd12-3d74f25db99c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-4813/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9b033bc2-a900-5699-a512-f1f9cfaa2f09" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-4813/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer-field/choices ["q-4813/selection/c05c767eb6742c0374517cb95a1cb5ab75783e23695ee9766c8351f9373f513d" "q-4813/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" "q-4813/selection/6758fbe0e699c4cf143d83ed08d339b0f33c0dcff4e60925d8c2187184bd9694" "q-4813/selection/f7ec98ce0d2d5e0413aaea93f098b04337f2217a14eff2f5b611bfb2fc659059" "q-4813/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-4813" :question/id #uuid "79f9d556-7f21-5f27-8c9c-efd0afeb41d2" :question/math-academy-id "q-4813" :question/problem "Let $f$ be a function such that ${f}^{′}(x)=2x$ and $f(2)=4.$ Use the tangent line approximation of $f(x)$ at $x=2$ to estimate the value of $f(3).$" :question/worked-solution "The tangent line approximation of $f(x)$ at the point $a=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(x) & =f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a) \\\\  & =f(2)+{f}^{′}(2)(x-2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that $f(2)=4,$ and since ${f}^{′}(x)=2x,$ then ${f}^{′}(2)=2(2)=4.$ So, the tangent line approximation is given by\n\n$$\nL(x)=4+4(x-2).\n$$\n\nNow, we can approximate $f(3)$ by evaluating the tangent line approximation at $x=3.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(3) & ≈L(3) \\\\  & =4+4(3-2) \\\\  & =4+4(1) \\\\  & =4+4 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-4813/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1b0dd714-5bf1-573f-9ff9-11802622ce92"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-4813"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-314900/field-1/48ebc16bb7d8920912c7b22d40a6a45380240b0df7ac9f534ba09da7b00ec380" :answer/id #uuid "63a15ade-af00-5457-b1c0-0b724a65271f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1+\\frac{\\pi\\sqrt{3}}{120}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-314900/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "4b69a7da-54d5-54d6-8299-518583d54e52" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-314900/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "d2b9ea2d-fcd1-5d14-8dc7-4e5d721697d8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-314900/field-1/48ebc16bb7d8920912c7b22d40a6a45380240b0df7ac9f534ba09da7b00ec380" :answer-field/choices ["q-314900/field-1/48ebc16bb7d8920912c7b22d40a6a45380240b0df7ac9f534ba09da7b00ec380" "q-314900/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-314900" :question/id #uuid "656c2c2e-203a-569b-a49f-ee98156b7c09" :question/math-academy-id "q-314900" :question/problem "Let $f$ be a function such that ${f}^{′}(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ and $f(\\frac{\\pi }{6})=1.$ Use the tangent line approximation of $f(x)$ at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ to estimate the value of $f(\\frac{\\pi }{5}).$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$f(\\frac{\\pi }{5})≈$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The tangent line approximation of $f(x)$ at the point $a=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(x) & =f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a) \\\\  & =f(\\frac{\\pi }{6})+{f}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{6})(x-\\frac{\\pi }{6}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that $f(\\frac{\\pi }{6})=1,$ and since ${f}^{′}(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{6})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}.\n$$\n\nSo, the tangent line approximation is given by\n\n$$\nL(x)=1+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}(x-\\frac{\\pi }{6}).\n$$\n\nNow, we can approximate $f(\\frac{\\pi }{5})$ by evaluating the tangent line approximation at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{5}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\frac{\\pi }{5}) & ≈L(\\frac{\\pi }{5}) \\\\  & =1+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}(\\frac{\\pi }{5}-\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =1+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{30} \\\\  & =1+\\frac{\\pi \\sqrt{3}}{120}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-314900/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1b0dd714-5bf1-573f-9ff9-11802622ce92"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-314900"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-4804"] :question/problem "Let $f$ be a function such that ${f}^{′}(x)={x}^{2}-4$ and $f(4)=13.$ Use the tangent line approximation of $f(x)$ at $x=4$ to estimate the value of $f(3.5).$" :question/worked-solution "The tangent line approximation of $f(x)$ at the point $a=4$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(x) & =f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a) \\\\  & =f(4)+{f}^{′}(4)(x-4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that $f(4)=13,$ and since ${f}^{′}(x)={x}^{2}-4,$ then ${f}^{′}(4)={4}^{2}-4=12.$ So, the tangent line approximation is given by\n\n$$\nL(x)=13+12(x-4).\n$$\n\nNow, we can approximate $f(3.5)$ by evaluating the tangent line approximation at $x=3.5.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(3.5) & ≈L(3.5) \\\\  & =13+12(3.5-4) \\\\  & =13+12(-0.5) \\\\  & =13-6 \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-48404/selection/e2119d70ad533224355534dbc8721438af5108f29e2c7c9201b0bcec5ece4905" :answer/id #uuid "511b45a1-d384-51c9-ac92-221d485ba9b2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$f(3.2)≈-2.2,$ an underestimate" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48404/selection/f5b11d7c29e0e3e78a98127e5348243956b55b4394d92c6c0b90f770708a8756" :answer/id #uuid "e3585176-e949-545e-866e-4695e64ab029" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$f(3.2)≈-3.4,$ an overestimate" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48404/selection/15388aa62bf615b4f6e20b896fcf02d0043878ccface9af1ff2b28dcf7ea1c76" :answer/id #uuid "d21e1eb4-e9ff-50df-8112-cea6047e76fa" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$f(3.2)≈-2.6,$ an overestimate" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48404/selection/b463caa75fcad39aad34822548169858d57e80b330af73b6919325e191a0e6da" :answer/id #uuid "06f026ca-0b10-5ace-a78e-a371958e13ea" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$f(3.2)≈-2.6,$ an underestimate" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48404/selection/074fa6c5633c43c9e2a972513b028663ff3193f5f844f5116efb94591abc931b" :answer/id #uuid "97b6af94-5134-5f68-954a-a24ee3931740" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$f(3.2)≈-2.2,$ an overestimate" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48404/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "144966e7-6f7d-5cfa-a5dd-f100857db0fb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-48404/selection/074fa6c5633c43c9e2a972513b028663ff3193f5f844f5116efb94591abc931b" :answer-field/choices ["q-48404/selection/e2119d70ad533224355534dbc8721438af5108f29e2c7c9201b0bcec5ece4905" "q-48404/selection/f5b11d7c29e0e3e78a98127e5348243956b55b4394d92c6c0b90f770708a8756" "q-48404/selection/15388aa62bf615b4f6e20b896fcf02d0043878ccface9af1ff2b28dcf7ea1c76" "q-48404/selection/b463caa75fcad39aad34822548169858d57e80b330af73b6919325e191a0e6da" "q-48404/selection/074fa6c5633c43c9e2a972513b028663ff3193f5f844f5116efb94591abc931b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-48404" :question/id #uuid "23fa4cab-6951-5a21-810d-7733098a8e5c" :question/math-academy-id "q-48404" :question/problem "The graph of the function $y=f(x)$ passes through $(3,-3)$ and is concave down on the interval $(1,4).$ If ${f}^{′}(3)=4,$ estimate the value of $f(3.2)$ using the tangent line approximation of $f(x)$ at $x=3$ and determine whether the approximation is an underestimate or overestimate." :question/worked-solution "The tangent line approximation of $f(x)$ at the point $a=3$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(x) & =f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a) \\\\  & =f(3)+{f}^{′}(3)(x-3).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function passes through the point $(3,-3),$ so we have $f(3)=-3.$ Also, we're told that ${f}^{′}(3)=4,$ so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(x) & =-3+4(x-3) \\\\  & =-3+4x-12 \\\\  & =4x-15.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can approximate $f(3.2)$ by evaluating the tangent line approximation at $x=3.2.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(3.2) & ≈L(3.2) \\\\  & =4(3.2)-15 \\\\  & =12.8-15 \\\\  & =-2.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since the function is concave down on the interval $(1,4),$ the linear approximation $L(x)$ is above the graph near $x=3,$ and therefore we have an overestimate." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-48404/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f542453-9758-55e6-93c6-6bfd2139ec45"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-48404"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-115269/selection/2a9379bdeb495c7bbd70e8f31060c2eb102a09a2d413c8603521217c7c255ee2" :answer/id #uuid "8fa905b1-8323-533a-9b78-678ebb482923" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$f(-2.9)≈-4.3,$ an underestimate" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115269/selection/ddef34680f4a5bcf5c32882693e57615d6cc8d27e80572a87a38cca6ee1b320d" :answer/id #uuid "02e0caa3-45a7-5dcf-bede-baaf50efb8f2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$f(-2.9)≈-3.7,$ an underestimate" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115269/selection/012eef575e39852c6a8f6f6682903e295a666f1b1927d5391a8a932644ec64fc" :answer/id #uuid "024a12f6-59f4-5bd3-b474-7bd6e2654b6c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$f(-2.9)≈-4.6,$ an underestimate" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115269/selection/f12f1b9a049c344ca53d46e95131c138d5d3a3127d7822fedbe87ff78fc9cdc8" :answer/id #uuid "7bca371b-8aae-573a-b7ae-7acb84677d7e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$f(-2.9)≈-4.3,$ an overestimate" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115269/selection/79705064f75045cbe5503008b504747a6d7b2f1201f0c11613a136abaabc9630" :answer/id #uuid "3cb82779-2d7a-50e5-b7e5-a6f21384b6ee" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$f(-2.9)≈-3.7,$ an overestimate" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115269/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "dacc59cc-937d-5a09-b84a-f5801d87553a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-115269/selection/79705064f75045cbe5503008b504747a6d7b2f1201f0c11613a136abaabc9630" :answer-field/choices ["q-115269/selection/2a9379bdeb495c7bbd70e8f31060c2eb102a09a2d413c8603521217c7c255ee2" "q-115269/selection/ddef34680f4a5bcf5c32882693e57615d6cc8d27e80572a87a38cca6ee1b320d" "q-115269/selection/012eef575e39852c6a8f6f6682903e295a666f1b1927d5391a8a932644ec64fc" "q-115269/selection/f12f1b9a049c344ca53d46e95131c138d5d3a3127d7822fedbe87ff78fc9cdc8" "q-115269/selection/79705064f75045cbe5503008b504747a6d7b2f1201f0c11613a136abaabc9630"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-115269" :question/id #uuid "e38e2288-7689-5ff9-a85e-e9b1eee01cc5" :question/math-academy-id "q-115269" :question/problem "The graph of the function $y=f(x)$ passes through $(-3,-4)$ and is concave down on the interval $(-4,-2).$ If ${f}^{′}(-3)=3,$ estimate the value of $f(-2.9)$ using the tangent line approximation of $f(x)$ at $x=-3$ and determine whether the approximation is an underestimate or overestimate." :question/worked-solution "The tangent line approximation of $f(x)$ at the point $a=-3$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(x) & =f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a) \\\\  & =f(-3)+{f}^{′}(-3)(x+3).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe graph of the function passes through the point $(-3,-4),$ so we have $f(-3)=-4.$ Also, we're told that ${f}^{′}(-3)=3,$ so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(x) & =-4+3(x+3) \\\\  & =-4+3x+9 \\\\  & =3x+5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can approximate $f(-2.9)$ by evaluating the tangent line approximation at $x=-2.9.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-2.9) & ≈L(-2.9) \\\\  & =3(-2.9)+5 \\\\  & =-8.7+5 \\\\  & =-3.7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since the function is concave down on the interval $(-4,-2),$ the linear approximation $L(x)$ is above the graph near $x=-3,$ and therefore we have an overestimate." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-115269/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f542453-9758-55e6-93c6-6bfd2139ec45"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-115269"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-115261/selection/c6eb046ccd76f0bc9d23633455bf5c707b70157094ac1deafb8e03cda2ab9829" :answer/id #uuid "92744a5f-f08c-58db-9382-8ed6b2c3210c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$f(x)$ has a global minimum at $x=\\sqrt{2}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115261/selection/8af4dfdb4cbc3e883e3a8ffffb33546800f61229e16fe6106e6af6d3006f492c" :answer/id #uuid "bbf57383-25d2-52e5-837b-7dd860dff200" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$f(x)$ has a local minimum at $x=\\sqrt{2}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115261/selection/6827190884906fbb3b05b561dc21109673e3bb17c7b8ad7dc5852c149a86cb74" :answer/id #uuid "b868e21c-5356-55f5-8804-a2e6df204c20" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$f(x)$ is concave down in the neighborhood of $x=\\sqrt{2}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115261/selection/c932d19bb123a5b6a30db543fee2df70b189907c1b418da777e39a6d4089a8f5" :answer/id #uuid "156a96f0-7771-57d8-b692-2fc348552bcb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$f(x)$ is concave up in the neighborhood of $x=\\sqrt{2}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115261/selection/f0af5b394d95510c7278ea6025d55267500f53dcebae2a61f6ca464fa7ab24ae" :answer/id #uuid "60b8f4aa-96c3-59fc-92af-6f6571d80dc1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$f(x)$ is a linear function" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115261/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "54487fe0-4811-5ed7-b1f8-8bc9f86a1dab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-115261/selection/6827190884906fbb3b05b561dc21109673e3bb17c7b8ad7dc5852c149a86cb74" :answer-field/choices ["q-115261/selection/c6eb046ccd76f0bc9d23633455bf5c707b70157094ac1deafb8e03cda2ab9829" "q-115261/selection/8af4dfdb4cbc3e883e3a8ffffb33546800f61229e16fe6106e6af6d3006f492c" "q-115261/selection/6827190884906fbb3b05b561dc21109673e3bb17c7b8ad7dc5852c149a86cb74" "q-115261/selection/c932d19bb123a5b6a30db543fee2df70b189907c1b418da777e39a6d4089a8f5" "q-115261/selection/f0af5b394d95510c7278ea6025d55267500f53dcebae2a61f6ca464fa7ab24ae"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-115261" :question/id #uuid "1aea0f50-2894-540a-8561-3e930ff1c7d7" :question/math-academy-id "q-115261" :question/problem "Given that the tangent line approximation to the function $f(x)$ at $x=\\sqrt{2}$ overestimates the values of the function in the neighborhood of $x=\\sqrt{2},$ which of the following must be true?" :question/worked-solution "Since the tangent line approximation of $f(x)$ at $x=\\sqrt{2}$ overestimates the values of the function, we have\n\n$$\nL(x)>f(x),\n$$\n\nthat is, the line $L(x)$ must be above the graph of $f(x)$ near the point  $x=\\sqrt{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the function must be concave down in the neighborhood of $x=\\sqrt{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-115261/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f542453-9758-55e6-93c6-6bfd2139ec45"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-115261"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186078885 :question/answer-fields 17592186076521] {:db/id "q-47782/selection/ma-v1/9b90771e59721f4fca7a6ff731e45a23d4ad163a394c20a0fffd674c0350da4d/7e5d73b3de0ad6423efffb3c001d83a0916fddda0219ee99da630341d38ac466" :answer/id #uuid "5382c60b-5782-59f9-b347-6a4b4981b7c9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$f(2.2)≈3.2,$ an overestimate" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47782/selection/ma-v1/9b90771e59721f4fca7a6ff731e45a23d4ad163a394c20a0fffd674c0350da4d/1104a7b6e003433ce6bc79a92d452c36245fd36feb2645945f965c9019db350a" :answer/id #uuid "be0d03de-732c-5293-8b0a-17a3b9375dc1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$f(2.2)≈2.8,$ an overestimate" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47782/selection/ma-v1/9b90771e59721f4fca7a6ff731e45a23d4ad163a394c20a0fffd674c0350da4d/261dfd55400f3bf0b4ab47c4af7037d3f7d3bd3078df029a485f977c5737b806" :answer/id #uuid "9ebf365b-db3d-5846-a855-93d6f13d4a6a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$f(2.2)≈2.9,$ an underestimate" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47782/selection/ma-v1/9b90771e59721f4fca7a6ff731e45a23d4ad163a394c20a0fffd674c0350da4d/510683f36dfd7b5cb735d3ce72cd0fb00b391c9ce757449a7e0054195e60c247" :answer/id #uuid "fb1094cd-e065-5c2c-98c6-a729d4d2b7a9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$f(2.2)≈3.2,$ an underestimate" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47782/selection/ma-v1/9b90771e59721f4fca7a6ff731e45a23d4ad163a394c20a0fffd674c0350da4d/d1059f6ecebbb4ff2cfb4c621ead87565e4fe2e1863d918eafe620ce498140f4" :answer/id #uuid "ef37adcf-c1d2-55cc-8144-87b9493493b8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$f(2.2)≈2.8,$ an underestimate" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-47782/selection/ma-v1/9b90771e59721f4fca7a6ff731e45a23d4ad163a394c20a0fffd674c0350da4d" :answer-field/id #uuid "60bbb7a0-b5a6-5d7b-b047-f1e3399886b0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-47782/selection/ma-v1/9b90771e59721f4fca7a6ff731e45a23d4ad163a394c20a0fffd674c0350da4d/d1059f6ecebbb4ff2cfb4c621ead87565e4fe2e1863d918eafe620ce498140f4" :answer-field/choices ["q-47782/selection/ma-v1/9b90771e59721f4fca7a6ff731e45a23d4ad163a394c20a0fffd674c0350da4d/7e5d73b3de0ad6423efffb3c001d83a0916fddda0219ee99da630341d38ac466" "q-47782/selection/ma-v1/9b90771e59721f4fca7a6ff731e45a23d4ad163a394c20a0fffd674c0350da4d/1104a7b6e003433ce6bc79a92d452c36245fd36feb2645945f965c9019db350a" "q-47782/selection/ma-v1/9b90771e59721f4fca7a6ff731e45a23d4ad163a394c20a0fffd674c0350da4d/261dfd55400f3bf0b4ab47c4af7037d3f7d3bd3078df029a485f977c5737b806" "q-47782/selection/ma-v1/9b90771e59721f4fca7a6ff731e45a23d4ad163a394c20a0fffd674c0350da4d/510683f36dfd7b5cb735d3ce72cd0fb00b391c9ce757449a7e0054195e60c247" "q-47782/selection/ma-v1/9b90771e59721f4fca7a6ff731e45a23d4ad163a394c20a0fffd674c0350da4d/d1059f6ecebbb4ff2cfb4c621ead87565e4fe2e1863d918eafe620ce498140f4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-47782"] :question/problem "The graph of the function $y=f(x)$ passes through $(2,3)$ and is concave up on the interval $(0,3).$ If ${f}^{′}(2)=-1,$ estimate the value of $f(2.2)$ using the tangent line approximation of $f(x)$ at $x=2$ and determine whether the approximation is an underestimate or overestimate." :question/worked-solution "The tangent line approximation of $f(x)$ at the point $a=2$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(x) & =f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a) \\\\  & =f(2)+{f}^{′}(2)(x-2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function passes through the point $(2,3),$ so we have $f(2)=3.$ Also, we're told that ${f}^{′}(2)=-1,$ so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(x) & =3+(-1)(x-2) \\\\  & =3-(x-2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can approximate $f(2.2)$ by evaluating the tangent line approximation at $x=2.2.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(2.2) & ≈L(2.2) \\\\  & =3-(2.2-2) \\\\  & =3-0.2 \\\\  & =2.8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since the function is concave up on the interval $(0,3),$ the linear approximation $L(x)$ is below the graph near $x=2,$ and therefore we have an underestimate." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-47782/selection/ma-v1/9b90771e59721f4fca7a6ff731e45a23d4ad163a394c20a0fffd674c0350da4d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-346718/field-1/0e8c61e1cbe5b6d4b3e52c0431e48b853c5faa01ca7ca0f5f9cf780292b06b1f" :answer/id #uuid "51901735-55ce-57ff-a203-e55d1e70c15c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-346718/field-1/c258b70821560c3c05fcb4407c110ff76fb2be43ff09a851c52ebb0455132f20" :answer/id #uuid "df19e00b-2f80-52c5-abdf-c15ff9d5815a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-346718/field-1/336de2bb8f0e1e5bec5444214921ab4007f840558e694e1651575347e5aed4f7" :answer/id #uuid "d24401ed-28e8-5083-9b98-653bc3ebf47d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-346718/field-1/2468d3f08d897d95f4d28b48c13e6034ce1716985d166fd89a0b8119476fe5c8" :answer/id #uuid "9ced8a26-e373-5b07-967f-75dbdcc2c2fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-346718/field-1/1ef14df341e2f354c34ae93e3c7ddfea65840e9fda1897b5ea50de018c5615fe" :answer/id #uuid "dbc2f0db-3b9f-54af-93d3-f64133c5e3bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-346718/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "72302244-010a-5afc-a1ec-6c20eb7383e0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-346718/field-1/0e8c61e1cbe5b6d4b3e52c0431e48b853c5faa01ca7ca0f5f9cf780292b06b1f" :answer-field/choices ["q-346718/field-1/0e8c61e1cbe5b6d4b3e52c0431e48b853c5faa01ca7ca0f5f9cf780292b06b1f" "q-346718/field-1/c258b70821560c3c05fcb4407c110ff76fb2be43ff09a851c52ebb0455132f20" "q-346718/field-1/336de2bb8f0e1e5bec5444214921ab4007f840558e694e1651575347e5aed4f7" "q-346718/field-1/2468d3f08d897d95f4d28b48c13e6034ce1716985d166fd89a0b8119476fe5c8" "q-346718/field-1/1ef14df341e2f354c34ae93e3c7ddfea65840e9fda1897b5ea50de018c5615fe"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-346718/field-2/b75f0df421c1d3c2be4949f3e1d65d645758732d10c6da03e9fdeb34a06af273" :answer/id #uuid "cfd45d72-5505-5a65-9ba7-8116bd4923b4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "underestimate" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-346718/field-2/0a4fb32c5ead7a42793f1609f7129a2d005c40f06f2ac02448bf0930df5b4d72" :answer/id #uuid "8e58b949-93b4-5760-9012-bc8688b6ea8e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "overestimate" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-346718/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "6906333d-7a6f-5997-b28d-26c43023e05e" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-346718/field-2/0a4fb32c5ead7a42793f1609f7129a2d005c40f06f2ac02448bf0930df5b4d72" :answer-field/choices ["q-346718/field-2/b75f0df421c1d3c2be4949f3e1d65d645758732d10c6da03e9fdeb34a06af273" "q-346718/field-2/0a4fb32c5ead7a42793f1609f7129a2d005c40f06f2ac02448bf0930df5b4d72"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-346718" :question/id #uuid "1e057b4a-7993-597c-ab2e-69625b21258e" :question/math-academy-id "q-346718" :question/problem "The graph of the function $y=f(x)$ passes through $(2,1)$ and is concave down on the interval $(1,4).$ If ${f}^{′}(2)=1,$ estimate the value of $f(1.6)$ using the tangent line approximation of $f(x)$ at $x=2$ and determine whether the approximation is an underestimate or overestimate.$\\,f(1.6)≈$ {{field-1}} and the approximation is an {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "The tangent line approximation of $f(x)$ at the point $a=2$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(x) & =f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a) \\\\  & =f(2)+{f}^{′}(2)(x-2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe graph of the function passes through the point $(2,1),$ so we have $f(2)=1.$ Also, we're told that ${f}^{′}(2)=1.$ So, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(x) & =1+1(x-2) \\\\  & =x-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can approximate $f(1.6)$ by evaluating the tangent line approximation at $x=1.6.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1.6) & ≈L(1.6) \\\\  & =1.6-1 \\\\  & =0.6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since the function is concave down on the interval $(1,4),$ the linear approximation $L(x)$ is above the graph near $x=2,$ and therefore we have an $\\text{overestimate}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-346718/field-1" "q-346718/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f542453-9758-55e6-93c6-6bfd2139ec45"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-346718"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-291"] :question/problem "Suppose that $f(-2) = 0$ and $f'(-2)=2.$ Estimate the value of $f(-1.8)$ using the tangent line approximation of $f(x)$ at $x=-2.$" :question/worked-solution "The tangent line approximation to $f(x)$ at the point $a=-2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(x) & =f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a) \\\\  & =f(-2)+{f}^{′}(-2)(x-(-2)) \\\\  & =0+2(x+2) \\\\  & =2(x+2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can approximate $f(-1.8)$ by evaluating the tangent line approximation at $x=-1.8.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-1.8) & ≈L(-1.8) \\\\  & =2(-1.8+2) \\\\  & =2(0.2) \\\\  & =0.4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-292"] :question/problem "Let $g$ be a function such that $g'(x) =\\sqrt{x}$ and $g(4) = 3.$ Using the tangent line approximation of $g(x)$ at $x=4,$ estimate the value of $g(3.6).$" :question/worked-solution "The tangent line approximation to $g(x)$ at the point $a=4$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(x) & =g(a)+{g}^{′}(a)(x-a) \\\\  & =g(4)+{g}^{′}(4)(x-4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that $g(4)=3,$ and since $g'(x)=\\sqrt{x},$ then $g'(4)=\\sqrt{4}=2.$ So, the tangent line approximation is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(x) & =3+2(x-4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can approximate $g(3.6)$ by evaluating the tangent line approximation at $x=3.6.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(3.6) & ≈L(3.6) \\\\  & =3+2(3.6-4) \\\\  & =3+2(-0.4) \\\\  & =3-0.8 \\\\  & =2.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-293"] :question/problem "The graph of the function $y=f(x)$ passes through $(-2,-5)$ and is concave down on the interval $(-\\infty,0).$ If $f'(-2)=3$, estimate the value of $f(-2.3)$ using the tangent line approximation of $f(x)$ at $x=-2$ and determine whether the approximation is an underestimate or overestimate." :question/worked-solution "The tangent line approximation to $f(x)$ at the point $a=-2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(x) & =f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a) \\\\  & =f(-2)+{f}^{′}(-2)(x-(-2)) \\\\  & =f(-2)+{f}^{′}(-2)(x+2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function passes through the point $(-2,-5),$ so we have $f(-2)=-5.$ Also, we're told that $f'(-2)=3,$ so we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(x) & =-5+3(x+2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can approximate $f(-2.3)$ by evaluating the tangent line approximation at $x=-2.3.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-2.3) & ≈L(-2.3) \\\\  & =-5+3(-2.3+2) \\\\  & =-5+3(-0.3) \\\\  & =-5-0.9 \\\\  & =-5.9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since the function is concave down on the interval $(-\\infty,0)$, the linear approximation $L(x)$ is above the graph near $x=-2,$ and therefore we have an overestimate." :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
